# Code standards

Python 3.12, `uv`, committed `uv.lock`, exact direct versions. Do not
`pip install`. Use `uv add`.

`ruff` rules: E, F, W, I, B, UP, SIM, RUF, N, PL. Line length 100.
`mypy --strict` on `src/`. `pytest --strict-markers`. Deterministic tests
with an explicit seed. `@pytest.mark.slow` still runs under `make check`.

Type hints everywhere in `src/`. Docstrings name units and point at the spec
section.

No broad `try/except`, silent fallback, or speculative helper. No checksum
or sha256 manifest. No notebooks in `src/` or `tasks/`. No live or paid LLM
call in the tests.

Numerical code uses numpy and scipy only once a spec section requires it.
Document matrix basis order. Prefer exact diagonalisation for references.

Task ids: `<family>_<nnn>_<slug>`. Scaffold with
`uv run python tools/new_task.py <task_id>`. Verifiers take tolerances from
`spec/TOLERANCES.md` by name. `make validate` must show the solution passing
and a do-nothing run failing.

`make check` is the local source of truth: fmt-check, lint, type, test,
validate.
